prompt.figure_latex_format:
All figure blocks follow the thesis's house style. Placement is always [H] (figures never float). Four variants are available; pick exactly one per approved figure per <layout_selection_rules>.

Variant 1 — Single figure (one image):

	\begin{figure}[H]
		\centering
		\includegraphics[width=0.7\textwidth]{Chapters/<chapter-num>-<chapter-slug>/sub-chapters/figures/<chapter-num>-<figure-slug>.png}
		\caption[<short caption for ToC>]{<long caption for body>. Adapted from \parencite{<key>}.}
		\label{fig:<figure-slug>}
	\end{figure}

Variant 2 — Horizontal stack (2-up or 3-up panels side by side):

	\begin{figure}[H]
		\centering
		\subfloat[<sub-caption a>.\label{fig:<sub-slug-a>}]{%
			\includegraphics[valign=t, width=0.45\textwidth]{Chapters/<chapter-num>-<chapter-slug>/sub-chapters/figures/<chapter-num>-<figure-slug-a>.png}%
		}
		\hfill
		\subfloat[<sub-caption b>.\label{fig:<sub-slug-b>}]{%
			\includegraphics[valign=t, width=0.45\textwidth]{Chapters/<chapter-num>-<chapter-slug>/sub-chapters/figures/<chapter-num>-<figure-slug-b>.png}%
		}
		\caption[<short caption for ToC>]{<long caption for body>. (a) <gloss of a>. (b) <gloss of b>. Adapted from \parencite{<key>}.}
		\label{fig:<group-slug>}
	\end{figure}

For 3-up: width=0.30\textwidth on each subfloat, \hfill between panels.

Variant 3 — Vertical stack (panels stacked top-to-bottom):

	\begin{figure}[H]
		\centering
		\subfloat[<sub-caption a>.\label{fig:<sub-slug-a>}]{%
			\includegraphics[width=0.7\textwidth]{Chapters/<chapter-num>-<chapter-slug>/sub-chapters/figures/<chapter-num>-<figure-slug-a>.png}%
		} \\
		\subfloat[<sub-caption b>.\label{fig:<sub-slug-b>}]{%
			\includegraphics[width=0.7\textwidth]{Chapters/<chapter-num>-<chapter-slug>/sub-chapters/figures/<chapter-num>-<figure-slug-b>.png}%
		}
		\caption[<short caption for ToC>]{<long caption for body>. (a) <gloss of a>. (b) <gloss of b>. Adapted from \parencite{<key>}.}
		\label{fig:<group-slug>}
	\end{figure}

Variant 4 — Grid (rows × columns; example shown for 2×2):

	\begin{figure}[H]
		\centering
		\subfloat[<sub-caption a>.\label{fig:<sub-slug-a>}]{%
			\includegraphics[valign=t, width=0.45\textwidth]{Chapters/<chapter-num>-<chapter-slug>/sub-chapters/figures/<chapter-num>-<figure-slug-a>.png}%
		}
		\hfill
		\subfloat[<sub-caption b>.\label{fig:<sub-slug-b>}]{%
			\includegraphics[valign=t, width=0.45\textwidth]{Chapters/<chapter-num>-<chapter-slug>/sub-chapters/figures/<chapter-num>-<figure-slug-b>.png}%
		} \\
		\subfloat[<sub-caption c>.\label{fig:<sub-slug-c>}]{%
			\includegraphics[valign=t, width=0.45\textwidth]{Chapters/<chapter-num>-<chapter-slug>/sub-chapters/figures/<chapter-num>-<figure-slug-c>.png}%
		}
		\hfill
		\subfloat[<sub-caption d>.\label{fig:<sub-slug-d>}]{%
			\includegraphics[valign=t, width=0.45\textwidth]{Chapters/<chapter-num>-<chapter-slug>/sub-chapters/figures/<chapter-num>-<figure-slug-d>.png}%
		}
		\caption[<short caption for ToC>]{<long caption for body>. (a)–(d) <glosses>. Adapted from \parencite{<key>}.}
		\label{fig:<group-slug>}
	\end{figure}

Width and spacing rules:
	- Variant 1 (Single): 0.7\textwidth (use 0.8 only when on-figure detail must remain legible at print size).
	- Variant 2 (Horizontal stack): 0.45\textwidth each for 2-up; 0.30\textwidth each for 3-up. Use \hfill between subfloats. Use valign=t to top-align panels of unequal height.
	- Variant 3 (Vertical stack): 0.7\textwidth each. Use `\\` between subfloats. valign is unnecessary because panels do not share a row.
	- Variant 4 (Grid): 0.45\textwidth each for 2×2; 0.30\textwidth each when any row has 3 columns. Use \hfill between columns and `\\` between rows. Use valign=t.

Slugs are lowercase, hyphenated, ≤4 words. Omit "Adapted from \parencite{<key>}." entirely when the figure is original to the thesis.

prompt.bibtex_format:
Newly minted BibTeX entries follow this house format:
- Citation key: lastnameYYYY_short_snake_case_title — first author's lowercase last name, year, three-to-five-word lowercase snake_case abbreviation of the title. - Indentation: a single tab before each field name. - Text fields wrapped in braces: {Title Here}. - Numeric fields unquoted: year = 2012. - Author lists in "Last, First and Last, First" form, separated by ` and `. - Online sources include url and urldate (YYYY-MM-DD). - Page ranges use --, e.g., pages = {15--28}.
Example: @inproceedings{zaharia2012_resilient_distributed_datasets, title = {Resilient Distributed Datasets: A Fault-Tolerant Abstraction for In-Memory Cluster Computing}, author = {Zaharia, Matei and Chowdhury, Mosharaf and Das, Tathagata and Dave, Ankur and Ma, Justin and McCauley, Murphy and Franklin, Michael J. and Shenker, Scott and Stoica, Ion}, year = {2012}, booktitle = {9th USENIX Symposium on Networked Systems Design and Implementation (NSDI 12)}, publisher = {USENIX Association}, address = {San Jose, CA}, pages = {15--28}, url = {https://www.usenix.org/conference/nsdi12/technical-sessions/presentation/zaharia}, urldate = {2026-04-29} }
